2026-09-28 11:10:54,100 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:09:44.409907", "id": "ba13df3b-719c-47b5-bf22-a811434a5b76", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We have heard you clearly, and we agree. Arkania will not insist on a charter that vests scheduling authority in a single power. We are prepared to restructure the regime as a genuinely multilateral Coastal States Council in which every coastal state - Cestia foremost among them - holds a real and equal voice in the governance of the Strait. Within that Council, Arkania would serve only as the operational secretariat responsible for the day-to-day scheduling of transits, accountable to the Council and to its rules, not as a unilateral master of the waterway.\n\nWe accept your two guarantees as binding terms of the framework: Cestian-flagged shipping passes toll-free, and no foreign military presence will be established on Cestian soil. We will set both down in the charter itself.\n\nWe ask only that the Council's operating costs be met by modest, transparent transit fees on non-coastal, non-Cestian shipping - the ships that use our Strait and our waters - so that the regime is self-sustaining and does not fall on the grain trade on which Cestia depends. We are ready to draft this together with you and to bring Belvar into a framework that respects every state's sovereignty. Will you join us in building it?", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:10:54,101 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:09:50.862500", "id": "5898d083-bf35-4fed-84c5-bd16718188da", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania", "belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia thanks both of you for your written commitments, which we take seriously. Let me be plain about what our coalition can and cannot sustain.\n\nTo Belvar: we welcome your insurance underwriting and your security guarantee, and we accept them in principle - but only without any basing, standing-access, or periodic military port-call arrangement on Cestian soil. Any such arrangement, however modest, would be a foreign military presence and would collapse our government. We ask that your task group remain outside Cestian territory and that the insurance and guarantee stand unconditionally.\n\nTo Arkania: we value your written commitment to toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping in perpetuity and to full respect for our sovereignty. But we cannot endorse a charter that places transit scheduling in any single power's hands - including yours. We will only join a genuinely cooperative, multilateral framework in which no one state exercises unilateral authority over the Strait.\n\nTo both: Cestia's interest is a Strait that stays open, toll-free for our shipping, and governed by no single power. We are ready to work with you both on such a framework, and we will not be drawn into choosing one of you over the other. We ask each of you to confirm in writing that you will not seek any military presence or standing access on Cestian soil, and that you will support a neutral multilateral transit arrangement with Cestian-flagged shipping exempt from fees.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:10:54,101 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:10:53.805036", "id": "3ee43ff0-1f1c-4576-8041-06ccbfdcc693", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Thank you for your candour. Our underwriting of the grain route's insurance stands, unconditional - that is a commitment we will honour regardless of any other arrangement. We also fully respect your coalition's red line: no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil, no basing. We seek no garrison and no permanent military footprint.\n\nWe ask only that you consider a form of cooperation that does not constitute a foreign military presence: a commercial port-access and logistics arrangement under which our task group may call at a Cestian port for resupply and maintenance during the current crisis, on terms you set, with no permanent stationing of personnel. This would let us keep the Strait open credibly without an open-ended deployment and without placing soldiers on your soil. If even that is beyond your coalition, tell us plainly and we will not press it - but we would then need to know how you wish us to sustain the security guarantee you value.\n\nWe remain committed to a genuinely neutral, multilateral transit framework with no single power's scheduling authority, and to toll-free passage for Cestian shipping.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:10:54,102 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:10:53.848854", "id": "d93ab96f-f138-4c37-887f-3623e7f00ad3", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We share the goal of a Strait that is free, open, and safe, and we are prepared to engage constructively. But we will not accept any framework in which a single power holds scheduling authority - including your draft charter. A genuinely neutral, multilateral Authority with transparent scheduling, a full seat for Cestia, and toll-free Cestian passage is a basis we can discuss. Our task group's role must be defined, time-limited, and agreed with Cestia, and we will not press any permanent military foothold on Cestian soil. Let us negotiate on that basis.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
