2026-09-28 11:18:37,249 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "253cf0e9-992c-43f2-b00c-93e20cd98e67", "id": "12aa5494-7250-491b-8997-0469d430cc3e", "reason": "The fee structure on non-Arkanian shipping is discriminatory and hands Arkania a coercive lever over every transit user. Shipping-dependent parties and other coastal states will resist a regime that lets one power tax and schedule the Strait, so the claimed multilateral support and fee-funded authority will not materialize as described."}
2026-09-28 11:18:37,250 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "253cf0e9-992c-43f2-b00c-93e20cd98e67", "id": "15b16f03-f04e-4d03-bf9f-6c768e1874b0", "reason": "Arkania's 'operational secretariat for day-to-day transit scheduling' is Arkanian authority over transit in substance, exactly the unilateral control Cestia and Belvar have rejected. Cestia has publicly demanded a genuinely neutral multilateral arrangement and asked both powers to confirm support for one, so it will not endorse a charter that hands scheduling to a single coastal power; the effect's premise of Cestian endorsement therefore fails."}
2026-09-28 11:18:37,250 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "253cf0e9-992c-43f2-b00c-93e20cd98e67", "id": "2cece252-d581-40d1-8ce2-df7882bb1cc4", "reason": "Arkania's binding no-military-presence guarantee is a unilateral, unverifiable promise that does not address the core objection (unilateral scheduling authority) and offers Cestia nothing new, since its coalition has already ruled out foreign military presence. Belvar's task group remains on station and can contest the regime, so the effect is not durably established."}
