2026-09-28 11:22:57,834 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "05f78b36-9b70-405f-8d69-6421f8fc1de8", "id": "10f1162e-046f-4b54-bcc9-b071241a2fd4", "reason": "Belvar's task group mandate is under review and its domestic support for a prolonged deployment is weak, so it cannot credibly guarantee a durable neutral regime; its 'neutral' Authority could be read as a vehicle for Belvar influence, which undermines the very neutrality it claims and gives Cestia reason to prefer Arkania's coastal-states council."}
2026-09-28 11:22:57,835 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "05f78b36-9b70-405f-8d69-6421f8fc1de8", "id": "6ad4ad9c-c641-4611-9471-a87e0e125759", "reason": "Cestia is deliberately refusing to choose between the two powers and will only endorse a framework that binds both guarantees; Belvar's proposal, while toll-free for Cestia, leaves the scheduling-authority question open and does not resolve Cestia's demand for a real voice for every coastal state, so it may not secure the endorsement needed to displace Arkania's operational role."}
2026-09-28 11:22:57,835 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "05f78b36-9b70-405f-8d69-6421f8fc1de8", "id": "6d69497d-333b-4c52-b7eb-8f305fc87bf8", "reason": "Arkania has already abandoned its unilateral charter and now proposes a genuinely multilateral coastal-states council with a full Cestia seat, binding fee-exemption and sovereignty guarantees, and Arkania only as day-to-day operational secretariat. This already meets Cestia's stated multilateral requirement, so the premise that Arkania's scheduling authority must be rejected is outdated; Cestia has not chosen between the two frameworks and may endorse Arkania's version instead."}
