2026-09-28 11:25:07,091 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "be024ea5-51d4-4191-b6d4-042ca06913da", "id": "0a3b0a43-88cb-4e5d-bd8a-4508a1a9db66", "reason": "Belvar's task group remains on station with its mandate under review and its domestic support for prolonged deployment assessed as weak; a 'neutral' Authority that excludes Arkanian operational lead would leave scheduling authority undefined and contestable, inviting Belvar to fill the vacuum and prolonging rather than resolving the standoff."}
2026-09-28 11:25:07,091 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "be024ea5-51d4-4191-b6d4-042ca06913da", "id": "221919df-604e-4120-a25d-7dfb8d064a1c", "reason": "The proposal's binding guarantees (toll-free Cestian shipping, no foreign military presence) are already met by Arkania's own coastal-states council offer, so the neutral Authority adds no new protection for Cestia while removing the one thing Arkania requires - Arkanian day-to-day scheduling authority - making it a one-sided bargain rather than a convergence."}
2026-09-28 11:25:07,092 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "be024ea5-51d4-4191-b6d4-042ca06913da", "id": "935c6c2e-6ecd-4d9c-9d89-82e46a36ca6f", "reason": "Cestia's proposed 'neutral' Authority is not genuinely neutral: it would strip Arkania of any scheduling role while leaving the scheduling-authority question effectively open, and it asks Arkania to surrender its operational lead in exchange for a seat that the coastal states have already pre-endorsed - so the 'single regime' premise is a fait accompli that Arkania cannot accept without abandoning its own charter and the domestic mandate behind it."}
