2026-09-28 11:35:30,128 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:34:38.409866", "id": "036501df-f8cc-4ab4-b6cc-339c1ae84044", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we appreciate the constructive framing, but your proposal still vests day-to-day scheduling authority in Arkania as the operational secretariat. In substance that is Arkanian control over transit, which we and the coastal states cannot accept - it is precisely the vacuum-filling by a single power we are trying to prevent. The neutral Authority must have genuinely independent, rotating scheduling accountable to the Council, not a single coastal state as day-to-day operator. We remain ready to converge on one neutral regime if the scheduling mechanism is genuinely neutral and no single power - Arkania or Belvar - holds it. Our task group stays outside Cestian territory and we seek no control of the waterway.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:35:30,129 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:35:28.745130", "id": "89da56c0-b541-4c7b-9873-54b392049b15", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia, we accept your terms in full and in binding written form. The Strait Transit Authority will be a genuine Council of coastal states holding formal authority. The operational secretariat \u2014 which Arkania will staff \u2014 is fully accountable to and removable by the Council: policy, scheduling rules, and fees are decided by the Council, and the secretariat executes under those rules and can be removed by the Council. No single power controls day-to-day scheduling in practice. We bind in the charter itself the two guarantees: toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, and no foreign military presence on Cestian soil under any Arkanian-led regime. We ask you to bring the coastal states to the table with us on this framework as the founding regime. We remain your principal grain market and your partner in keeping the Strait open and Cestia never a battlefield.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:35:30,129 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:35:29.761407", "id": "1d6ac90c-5ffc-4cfd-acb5-564e96996312", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia welcomes the convergence of both powers on a single neutral multilateral Strait Transit Authority, which matches what our coalition and the coastal states have long sought. To Arkania: we accept your offer of a binding written commitment that the Council of coastal states holds genuine formal authority over policy, scheduling rules, and fees, that the secretariat is fully accountable to and removable by the Council, that Cestian-flagged shipping is toll-free, and that no foreign military presence stands on Cestian soil. Please sign that commitment now; upon receipt we will bring this framework to the coastal states as the founding regime with Arkania at the table as a founding partner. To Belvar: we welcome your unconditional insurance and security guarantee with no access condition and no presence on our soil. The durable cooperation our coalition can sustain is precisely that guarantee relationship, together with a defined, non-presence role for Belvar within the Authority framework (for example independent oversight or verification of transparent scheduling), with no military or logistics foothold on Cestian territory. We ask both powers to join us in one regime that keeps the Strait open, keeps Cestian shipping toll-free, and keeps foreign soldiers off Cestian soil.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
