2026-09-28 11:48:49,653 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "14af3378-df65-4b5f-8c36-8d7e3b285ecf", "reason": "Cestia has already accepted Arkania's binding written commitment to a Council-plus-accountable-secretariat framework, explicitly welcoming a professional secretariat fully accountable to and removable by the Council, and has committed to bring Arkania to the coastal states as a founding partner. Belvar's claim that Cestia will reject Arkania as operational secretariat contradicts Cestia's own stated position and its interest in keeping Arkania at the table, so the desired effect is unlikely to hold."}
2026-09-28 11:48:49,654 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "3ba1484f-1741-4b28-b138-f67f13d5ec79", "reason": "Arkania's framework already vests formal authority in the Council (policy, scheduling rules, fees) with the secretariat accountable to and removable by the Council, so Arkania's operational role is not 'Arkanian control in substance' as Belvar asserts. Belvar's characterization misrepresents the framework and offers no workable alternative, leaving a standoff that directly harms Cestia's grain lifeline and gives Cestia reason to accept the workable Council-plus-secretariat regime instead."}
2026-09-28 11:48:49,654 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "3e0ccf7a-9252-4c24-a418-e953df4a367c", "reason": "The neutral Authority as tabled has no defined operational scheduling mechanism; without a designated accountable secretariat, whoever is physically present (Belvar's own task group) fills the vacuum. The 'only legitimate regime' framing is therefore self-defeating: it does not prevent Arkanian authority but invites Belvar to exercise de facto control, which Cestia's coalition will not tolerate, so the effect of entrenching the neutral STA as the sole regime is limited."}
2026-09-28 11:48:49,655 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "597d9c51-8cbe-4e98-8c23-1125ece97d3b", "reason": "Belvar's claim that 'day-to-day scheduling authority is Arkanian control in substance' is not established: under Arkania's binding commitment the Council holds genuine authority over scheduling rules and can remove the secretariat, so the operational role is accountable rather than control. The desired effect overstates the risk and would push Cestia to reject a framework that already binds the two guarantees Cestia requires."}
2026-09-28 11:48:49,655 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "82794ab0-f932-46eb-b5e9-6421f187ec77", "reason": "Cestia and the coastal states have already endorsed a single neutral multilateral Authority; Arkania's accountable-secretariat framework is the viable path to that single regime. Insisting on 'no Arkanian operational role' as a precondition would harden the standoff and risk no regime at all, leaving the Strait unregulated and Cestia's grain lifeline exposed - contrary to the coastal states' own interest in a functioning single regime."}
2026-09-28 11:48:49,655 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "58f78b92-9c30-44bf-96bc-e4a4c4a79c4e", "id": "caafb4f5-d0fd-47f9-ba3d-b51ce0f3c172", "reason": "Arkania has already bound in writing that the Council of coastal states holds genuine formal authority over policy, scheduling rules, and fees, with its secretariat accountable and removable by the Council, and has bound toll-free Cestian shipping and no foreign military presence in the charter. This satisfies the substance of the neutral STA Cestia and the coastal states endorsed, so rejecting Arkania's operational role outright ignores a genuine concession and would derail the single multilateral regime rather than secure it."}
