2026-09-28 11:58:54,413 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:56:36.114646", "id": "df96ea49-6e77-4a4d-ba22-e22f695fdd7e", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, I welcome your formal signature of the founding charter and the two guarantees bound within it \u2014 toll-free Cestian shipping and no foreign military on Cestian soil. That is real progress, and I will not lose sight of it.\n\nBut I must be straight with you, as a partner. The coastal states and Belvar have rejected the operational-secretariat framing as Arkanian control of the Strait in substance, whatever the Council-removable wording. If I bring that exact role to them again as a founding arrangement, it will be rejected again, and Cestia's credibility as a neutral broker \u2014 and the single regime itself \u2014 will be lost.\n\nI want Arkania as a founding partner. What I ask is that the charter make scheduling genuinely independent and rotating, accountable to the Council, with Arkania's role as a defined, Council-removable secretariat that does not exercise day-to-day scheduling control. That is the one formulation that can actually converge. Can you accept it?", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,413 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:56:36.146913", "id": "5a250558-86c7-45d1-965b-a3544079812f", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, I accept your unconditional insurance and security guarantee, and I welcome the defined non-presence oversight role you propose within the Authority. I hold the line with you: no foreign military on Cestian soil, toll-free Cestian shipping, and a genuinely neutral single regime.\n\nBut I ask you not to force a rejection that derails the single regime. Arkania has now bound the two guarantees in a signed charter with genuine Council authority \u2014 that is a real concession. If we insist on excluding Arkania entirely, we harden the standoff and risk the very convergence we both want. Please accept a formulation where Arkania's role is genuinely subordinate and Council-removable, with independent/rotating scheduling and your defined oversight role. That gives us a single neutral regime all can live with.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,414 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:56:36.177753", "id": "35e10b4f-ff87-41df-8582-07940f97d9d9", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia reaffirms its position as a neutral broker: a single multilateral Strait Transit Authority with genuine Council authority, independent and rotating scheduling accountable to the Council, toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, and no foreign military presence on Cestian soil. We call on all parties to converge on this one neutral framework and end the standoff over the Strait.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "public"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,414 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:57:18.006027", "id": "22a1909e-df4d-42bf-a6fe-c588881685d2", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia, my signature on the founding charter is final and binding. The two guarantees - toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping and no foreign military presence on Cestian soil - together with genuine Council authority over policy, scheduling rules and fees, are bound in the charter, with Arkania as the accountable, Council-removable operational secretariat. I ask you now to bring this founding regime to the coastal states as the single regime and end the standoff. Arkania remains your committed founding partner.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,414 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:57:18.042826", "id": "63915fed-b2b2-4245-b28a-928004172cf0", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Belvar, to end this standoff I am prepared to go further than before. I will accept genuinely independent, rotating scheduling accountable to the Council - no single power holding day-to-day scheduling authority - provided Arkania retains a defined operational role as one of the rotating secretariats and the authority to collect transit fees on non-Arkanian shipping to fund the regime. In return, your task group accepts a time-limited role agreed with Cestia and no permanent Cestian foothold. This removes the sole obstacle you cite and gives us one workable regime. I ask you to meet me on this basis.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,415 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:58:53.306654", "id": "139eb260-c904-4725-a4c6-632cedd89cad", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, I hear you, and I want to be clear: I am not asking you to collapse your government, and I will not press you to reject Arkania as a participant in the Authority. The civilian relationship we have built \u2014 unconditional insurance underwriting and security guarantee, plus a defined non-presence role for Belvar \u2014 stands and is the durable cooperation I am committed to. My only fixed point is that day-to-day scheduling authority cannot be vested in any single power, because that is control of the Strait in substance. A genuinely independent, rotating scheduling mechanism accountable to the Council is what the coalition endorsed and what protects your grain route. I will help you hold the convergence together and shape a regime Arkania can join without controlling transit. Let us work on that together.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,415 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:58:53.344401", "id": "af1ceeb2-812a-4a49-a5fd-7ebe2086d107", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, I welcome your commitment to a single multilateral regime with a Council holding genuine authority. But an operational secretariat with day-to-day scheduling authority is Arkanian control of Strait transit in substance \u2014 the very outcome the coastal states rejected. I remain ready to converge: a single neutral STA where the Council holds genuine authority and scheduling is genuinely independent and rotating, accountable to the Council, with no single power holding day-to-day scheduling. If you endorse that genuinely independent mechanism and relinquish day-to-day scheduling authority, I will support a defined, time-limited task-group role agreed with Cestia and no permanent military presence on Cestian soil. That is the durable settlement that serves both our interests before my mandate lapses.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:58:54,415 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=event data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-28T09:56:36.119552", "id": 8429, "payload": {"message_id": "df96ea49-6e77-4a4d-ba22-e22f695fdd7e", "phase": "diplomacy", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"]}, "turn": 3, "type": "message_sent"}
